bar (1.6 MPa)\", \"hot_water\": same}\n- {\"attribute\": \"pressure_loss_class\", ...: \"0.63 bar (0.063 MPa)\"}\n- {\"attribute\": \"environmental_class\", ...: \"B, C\"}\n\nHmm the original text: \"0,1 °C bis 30 °C\" — German \"bis\". I'll render \"0.1 °C to 30 °C\".\n\nTemperature classes row: span both — I'll put in both columns.\n\nOK — also the pressure loss class: \"0,63 bar (0,063 MPa)\" → \"0.63 bar (0.063 MPa)\".\n\nNow type_level details:\n\n\"temperature_range_cold_water\": {\"value\": {\"min\": 0.1, \"max\": 30}, \"unit_symbol\": \"°C\", \"unit_id\": null, \"footnote_markers\": []}\n\"temperature_range_hot_water\": {\"value\": {\"min\": 30, \"max\": 90}, ...}\n\"maximum_permitted_error_cold_upper_zone\": {\"value\": 2, \"unit_symbol\": \"%\"} with maybe reference note? Schema doesn't support reference field in type_level; label encodes it: \"maximum_permitted_error_cold_q2_to_q4\". Use that.\n\"maximum_permitted_error_cold_q2_to_q4\": {\"value\": 2, \"unit_symbol\": \"%\"}\n\"maximum_permitted_error_cold_q1_to_q2\": {\"value\": 5, \"unit_symbol\": \"%\"}\n\"maximum_permitted_error_hot_q2_to_q4\": {\"value\": 3, \"unit_symbol\": \"%\"}\n\"maximum_permitted_error_hot_q1_to_q2\": {\"value\": 5, \"unit_symbol\": \"%\"}\n\"temperature_class\": {\"value\": \"T30 / T50 / T70 / T90\", \"unit_symbol\": null}\n\"pressure_range\": {\"value\": {\"min\": 0.3, \"max\": 16}, \"unit_symbol\": \"bar\"}\n\"pressure_range_mpa\": {\"value\": {\"min\": 0.03, \"max\": 1.6}, \"unit_symbol\": \"MPa\"}\n\"pressure_loss_class\": {\"value\": {\"min\": null, \"max\": 0.63}, \"unit_symbol\": \"bar\"}\n\"environmental_class\": {\"value\": \"B, C\", \"unit_symbol\": null}\n\"q2_over_q1_ratio\": {\"value\": 1.6, \"unit_symbol\": null}\n\nGood.\n\nShould footnote_markers be included as empty arrays everywhere? Schema shows footnote_markers in the value object shape. I'll include footnote_markers only when non-empty to reduce noise... The rule 2 shape includes footnote_markers key. I'll